{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Future of Old Age", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Silent Syllables in Which Unstressed Vowels are not Pronounced ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>Syllables are the sound groupings in words. </p><p>For example:<br/>Ca - na - da <br/>Com - pu - ter</p><p>Usually, you pronounce each syllable in a word.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some words in English have syllables which are not pronounced.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some examples are:<br/> vegetable  ----->  veg**table<br/> chocolate -----> choc**late<br/> diamond ------> di**mond<br/> interesting ----> int**resting<br/>dangerous -----> dang**rous", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the words above. Clap each time you say a syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "People are living longer because of better nutrition (more vegetables, less chocolate - or at least the right kind of chocolate, a glass of red wine a day).", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For some in the medical community, their lofty, but interesting goal is to redefine the very nature of human life. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This is the most dangerous of all pursuits, isn't it? ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Words That End in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In English, many words share similar endings. One common ending is <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Generally, when a word ends with the vowel <span class=\"strong\">e</span>, the vowel that comes before it is pronounced with its long sound. You can see this rule when you read and say words that end in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>f - <span class=\"strong\">i</span> - n - <span class=\"strong\">e</span>  ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">i</span> (as in the word <span class=\"italic\">eye</span>)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use this rule with other words and for other sounds. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>g - <span class=\"strong\">a</span> - m- <span class=\"strong\">e</span> ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">a</span> (as in the word <span class=\"italic\">day</span>)<br/>b - <span class=\"strong\">o</span> - n - <span class=\"strong\">e</span> ----> the word is pronounced with the long vowel sound for the letter <span class=\"strong\">o</span> (as in the word <span class=\"italic\">go</span>)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here are some examples of words that end in <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span>.<br/><span class=\"italic\">fine <br/>dine <br/>wine <br/>line <br/>redefine <br/>shine <br/>deadline <br/>divine</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading these sentences aloud. Focus on the pronunciation of the <span class=\"italic\">-ine</span> sound.<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>It should remain up to the div<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> powers. </li><li>Their lofty, but interesting goal is to redef<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> the very nature of human life.  </li><li>To answer that question and to sh<span class=\"italic\">ine</span> a light on the issue, we need to reconsider our conventional notion of life.</li><li>A glass of red w<span class=\"strong\">ine</span> a day ...</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "conventional ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "traditional; related to tradition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to re-examine our conventional notion of how we live, how we age, and when we die. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about staying healthy.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "notion ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "idea; point of view", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to re-examine our conventional notion of how we live, how we age, and when we die.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "life expectancy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the projected duration of a person's life ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the last hundred years, life expectancy has increased.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "philosopher ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who studies topics related to ethics or metaphysics", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Philosophers have looked for a fountain of youth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "diamond wedding anniversary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a celebration of the 60th year of marriage ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We all want to reach our diamond wedding anniversary.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lofty ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very high; eminent", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Their lofty but interesting goal is to redefine the nature of human life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "immortality ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the condition of perpetual life", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: However, there are many people who have questions about whether immortality should even be considered.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pursuit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of looking for something, especially a goal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Integrating humans and technology to create immortals is a dangerous pursuit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Find the movie <span class=\"italic\">The Terminator</span> online or at your video store.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "As you watch the movie, think about the idea of integrating technology and humans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss the movie and the implications it has for the future of old age.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">The Terminator</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I consider the idea of integrating technology and humans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the movie with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "What is the future of old age? To answer that question and to shine a light on\nthe issue, we need to re-examine our conventional notion of how we live, how we age, and\nwhen we die. In the last hundred years, life expectancy has increased. In fact, it has doubled.  People live to a more advanced age because of better nutrition (more vegetables, less chocolate - or at least the right kind of chocolate, a glass of wine a day), healthier\nlifestyles, and incredible advances in healthcare and medical science."}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img02.jpg", "time": "30000", "id": 2, "text": "Philosophers, doctors, and scientists have been striving for that fountain of youth since the beginning of recorded history. We all want to live forever, right? We all want to reach our diamond wedding anniversary, don't we? For some in the medical community, their lofty, but interesting aim is to reformulate the current concept of human life. Their research focuses on extending the deadline of the human lifespan, extending our lives by decades, centuries or more. However, there are many people who have questions about whether immortality should even be considered - that it should remain up to the divine powers."}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "62000", "id": 3, "text": "The newest and most ambitious ideas are about integrating humans and technology\nto create beings that can live for thousands of years. We've all seen <span class=\"italic\">The Terminator</span>, haven't we? This is the most dangerous of all pursuits, isn't it?"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le12ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le12ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can say and use words like <span class=\"italic\">fine</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can say 